<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- MainWindow — the app shell. The map fills the whole window; the UI is a MENU BAR over its top edge, a vertical
     MAP-TOOLS RAIL down its left (or beside the left temporal pane), a small FLOATING pane selector per map pane and the
     FLOATING radar console. There is NO bottom chrome (2026-11-04).

       ┌ Atlas View Settings Temporal Mode Pane Mode Isolation ── [ Search places ✕ ⌕ ] ── drag ── – □ ✕ ┐  TOP MENU BAR
       ├──┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  (always shown,
       │◗▸│                           ┃                              │  no tab); search CENTRED, its box + margins
       │▤▸│              ╭─────────╮┃╭─────────╮                   │  set the bar's height (46)
       │⁘ │  map pane 2  │SRV ▓▒░  │┃│CC  ▓▒░  │   map pane 3      │  FLOATING PANE SELECTORS — product, colour-ramp
       │⛶ ├━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╋━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┤  legend, tilt. Quad shown: all four at the
       │↻ │              │Ref ▓▒░  │┃│Vel ▓▒░  │                   │  CROSSING; two across = against the divider;
       │⁘ │              ╰─────────╯┃╰─────────╯                   │  single = centred under the bar.
       │◍ │  map pane 0  (MAIN)     ┃        map pane 1            │  View → Pane selectors hides all.
       │⊚ │                  ╭────────────────────╮           │  SITE TAB (RadarConsoleSiteTab) — home +
       │⁘ │                  │ ⌂ KTLX Oklahoma ˅  │           │  favorites, centred on the console's top
       │⌕ │       ╭──────────┴────────────────────┴─────────╮ │  FLOATING RADAR CONSOLE (2026-11-03) —
       │◎▸│       │ 1:07 PM ═══ scrubber ═══ ◀ ▶ ▶ ↺  VCP: 212 │ │  rounded, centred (play = the midpoint),
       │  │       │ 2 min ago      3/10        Mode: precip   │ │  SelectorGap above the window bottom.
       │  │       ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯ │  View → Radar console. Site needed.
       └──┴──────────────────────── ↑ window midpoint ─────────────┘
        ↑ the MAP-TOOLS RAIL (2026-11-04): radar networks · map layers · fit · reset north · markers · location ·
          inspect · rings/ruler, CENTRED top to bottom;
          on the window's left edge, DOCKED to the NowCast / PastCast pane's right edge while one shows (TEMPORAL PANES block).

          ↑ NO RULES ANYWHERE — every seam is a soft SHADOW instead, drawn by whichever side owns it: the top bar casts its
            own down, the rail its own onto the map; the floating selectors and the console cast rounded halos.
          ↑ THE BOTTOM TOOLS STRIP IS GONE (2026-11-04, the user's call): its map tools became the left RAIL
            (Composites/MapControlsStrip, vertical now); its pane-layout key became the top bar's PANE MODE menu and its
            isolation picker the top bar's ISOLATION item. So the temporal panes and the rail run to the window bottom.
          ↑ The console never shrinks; in a narrow window it overlaps the panes' bottoms (it is declared after them).
          ↑ [⌂ KTLX ˅] = the SITE PICKER (home + favorites), the console's centred TAB (back 2026-11-04, after a day as the
            centre of a console top row whose other tools moved to the rail). It replaced the old bar's Home key AND the side
            car that used to hang off the Atlas key — two doors to one list. See Composites/RadarConsoleSiteTab. Don't
            re-add a Home key.
          ↑ Atlas, Settings and the temporal modes are TOP MENU BAR items (2026-11-03); activity shows in each temporal
            pane's ACTIVITY EXPANDER (TemporalPaneActivityExpander, 2026-10-16).
          ↑ Not drawn above: the LOOP HOLDING GATE — while a PastCast loop loads, the whole map (notches included; the top
            bar, the rail and the console paint over it) is frosted behind "Loading the loop" + progress bars + Cancel load
            (no escape since 2026-10-10). See Composites/LoopHoldingGate.

     ⚠️ WHAT REPEATS PER PANE IS NOT IN THE BAR ANY MORE. It used to be: the bar's left cluster carried a
     160px "chip" per pane (a combined product-selector-and-colour-ramp) plus the one tilt combo, which is
     what made the bar's left half a width BUDGET that the centred temporal keys had to be defended from.
     Both moved into the pane notches — where the legend sits on the field it describes — so the bar's left
     is now just the global time module and the chip's width floor is gone with it. Add a PER-PANE control
     to PaneNotchContent; add a GLOBAL one to RadarControls or to the right cluster here.

     ⚠️ THE PANE WATERMARK IS GONE TOO (the big ghosted "Ref" in a pane's corner). The notch says the same
     thing better, a few pixels away. See the PANE NOTCHES block below.

     ⚠️ The bar has NO keys of its own now (2026-11-03) — the console only. Square keys elsewhere still follow
     Controls/Styles.xaml, section 2.

     The bar's CENTER is RadarControls (the global time module), held on the bar's midpoint by a [*, Auto, *] grid;
     both sides are BLANK since 2026-11-03 (temporal keys, Atlas, Settings → the top menu bar).

     ⚠️ THE KEYS IN THIS CLUSTER take their LOOK from ONE style chain in Controls/Styles.xaml
     (BarChromeButtonStyle → BarKeyToggleStyle for the ones that latch / BarIconButtonStyle for the one
     that acts): hairline at rest, accent BORDER + raised face when ON, and the SAME SQUARE, set by that
     chain from the shared BarKeySide — ONE home for the look. (The bar itself holds no keys now; BarKeySide
     still pins its height.)
     ⚠️ SIZES ARE DECLARED, NOT MEASURED. They used to be: each cluster measured the height its row was
     given and mirrored it onto Width, because the per-pane product chips lived in the bar and changed its
     height. The chips moved to the pane notches and the whole apparatus (a Layout/BarKeyMetrics class, two
     SizeChanged handlers, a name-font probe) was deleted — read the ⚠️ history in Styles.xaml section 2
     before reviving any of it. Nothing here should set a size, corner radius or font per instance unless
     that key is the ONLY consumer of it (the pane key's wide mark, in this file's own Resources) — per-
     instance attributes are what put ~40 duplicated values in this file before.
     The transport buttons in RadarControls are the one cluster still on the old stock look.

     ⚠️ THE TOP BAR IS BACK (the user's call, 2026-11-01) — as a MENU bar this time (View menu, the window's caption
     drag run, – □ ✕), with its own centred "Menu" tab to hide it, so the stripe of map it covers is the user's
     choice. (A full-width top bar existed once to hold per-window controls, and went because the band was pure cost.)
     The pane notches are now FLOATING pane selectors — see the PANE NOTCHES block. -->
     <!-- TOP OF WINDOW (2026-11-01):
       ┌ View ──────────────────────── drag ───────────────────────── – □ ✕ ┐
       ├──────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────┤
       │ PastCast │      ╭────────────────╮                    │ ForeCast │  temporal panes under the bar,
       │ /NowCast │      │Ref˅│▓▒░▒▓│0.5°│  a floating pane    │          │  selectors floating (see below)
       │          │      ╰────────────────╯  selector           │          │
     -->
<Window
    x:Class="Anvil.MainWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:Anvil"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    xmlns:controls="using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls"
    xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
    xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
    xmlns:ctl="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
    xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
    xmlns:tp="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes"
    mc:Ignorable="d"
    Title="Anvil">

    <!-- ONE overlay cell over the whole window (the bottom chrome row went 2026-11-04; the leftover Grid.RowSpan="2"s are
         harmless). The map fills it; the top bar, the TEMPORAL PANES + the MAP-TOOLS RAIL, the pane selectors and the
         floating console overlay it. Every other panel that pops over the map is a real top-level OS window owned by
         WindowManager. -->
    <Grid x:Name="RootGrid" Background="#FF0A0A0A">
        <!-- ===== FULL SCREEN (the user's call, 2026-11-04) — the animations and keys; the rules are at MainWindow.xaml.cs
             FULL SCREEN. F11 toggles; Esc leaves (never while typing); both also arrive from the MAP via map.js HOST KEYS,
             because a focused WebView swallows them. ===== -->
        <Grid.KeyboardAccelerators>
            <KeyboardAccelerator Key="F11" Invoked="OnFullScreenAccelerator"/>
            <KeyboardAccelerator Key="Escape" Invoked="OnEscapeAccelerator"/>
        </Grid.KeyboardAccelerators>
        <Grid.Resources>
            <!-- The top bar slides like the auto-hidden Windows taskbar: a quick ease-out down, a quicker one away. The
                 slide-OUT's To is the bar's measured height (set in code, HideTopBar). -->
            <Storyboard x:Key="TopChromeSlideIn">
                <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="TopChromeSlide" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Y" To="0" Duration="0:0:0.2">
                    <DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                        <ExponentialEase EasingMode="EaseOut" Exponent="5"/>
                    </DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                </DoubleAnimation>
            </Storyboard>
            <Storyboard x:Key="TopChromeSlideOut">
                <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="TopChromeSlide" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Y" To="-60" Duration="0:0:0.15">
                    <DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                        <ExponentialEase EasingMode="EaseIn" Exponent="4"/>
                    </DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                </DoubleAnimation>
            </Storyboard>
            <!-- The hint on entering full screen: fades in, holds ~3 s, fades out. -->
            <Storyboard x:Key="FullScreenHintFlash">
                <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="FullScreenHint" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                    <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0" Value="0"/>
                    <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.2" Value="1"/>
                    <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:3.2" Value="1"/>
                    <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:3.7" Value="0"/>
                </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
            </Storyboard>
        </Grid.Resources>

        <!-- Full-window map (bottom layer; the bar floats on top of it). -->
        <controls:WebView2 x:Name="MainMapWebView" Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2">
            <!-- The SITE MENU — what a site key's chevron opens (RadarSiteMenu.cs describes it per open; the
                 code-behind's OnRadarSiteMenuRequested fills these items' labels and shows it under the key).
                 ⚠️ ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False" (windowed), like every flyout here — else the owned
                 panel windows paint over it. -->
            <FlyoutBase.AttachedFlyout>
                <MenuFlyout x:Name="SiteMenu" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                    <!-- Header: the site's name, its status words on the right. Disabled — it is a title. -->
                    <MenuFlyoutItem x:Name="SiteMenuHeader" IsEnabled="False"/>
                    <MenuFlyoutSeparator/>
                    <!-- "Unload radar" on the loaded site; greyed (reason on the right) when offline. -->
                    <MenuFlyoutItem x:Name="SiteMenuLoad" Click="OnSiteMenuLoad">
                        <MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                            <SymbolIcon x:Name="SiteMenuLoadIcon" Symbol="Play"/>
                        </MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                    </MenuFlyoutItem>
                    <MenuFlyoutItem Text="Open in Atlas" Click="OnSiteMenuAtlas">
                        <MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                            <SymbolIcon Symbol="Map"/>
                        </MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                    </MenuFlyoutItem>
                    <MenuFlyoutSeparator/>
                    <MenuFlyoutItem x:Name="SiteMenuHome" Click="OnSiteMenuHome">
                        <MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                            <SymbolIcon Symbol="Home"/>
                        </MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                    </MenuFlyoutItem>
                    <MenuFlyoutItem x:Name="SiteMenuFavorite" Click="OnSiteMenuFavorite">
                        <MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                            <SymbolIcon x:Name="SiteMenuFavoriteIcon" Symbol="Favorite"/>
                        </MenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                    </MenuFlyoutItem>
                </MenuFlyout>
            </FlyoutBase.AttachedFlyout>
        </controls:WebView2>

        <!-- ===== PANE NOTCHES — now FLOATING PANE SELECTORS (the user's call, 2026-11-01) =====
             One per pane: a small FLOATING box holding everything that describes THAT pane — its product, its
             colour-ramp legend, its tilt. Attached to nothing (OverlayBar IsFloating: every corner rounded), no tab
             of its own: the top bar's View → Pane selectors shows / hides all four (ArePaneSelectorsVisible).
             PLACEMENT is MainWindow.PlacePaneSelectors (code: it depends on the top bar's measured height), 8 px gaps:

             SINGLE                         TWO ACROSS                       QUAD
             ════════ top bar ════════      ════════ top bar ════════        ═════════ top bar ═════════
                 ╭───────────────╮          ╭──────────╮┃╭──────────╮        ┃         ┃
                 │Ref˅│▓▒░▒▓│0.5°│          │Ref ▓▒░ 0.5°│┃│Vel ▓▒░ 0.5°│     ╭──────╮┃╭──────╮
                 ╰───────────────╯          ╰──────────╯┃╰──────────╯        │ SRV  │┃│  CC  │   top row: hangs
                 centred, under the bar     against the divider, under      ━━━━━━━━━━╋━━━━━━━━━━   UP (Edge Bottom)
                                            the bar                          │ Ref  │┃│ Vel  │   bottom row: DOWN
                                                                             ╰──────╯┃╰──────╯   all at the crossing
             (The top bar has no Menu tab since 2026-11-04, so it is always there to sit under.)

             ⚠️ THE WATERMARK IS GONE. Each pane used to carry a big ghosted product label in its top-left
             corner, because every control lived in the bottom bar and the pane had no other way to say what
             it was showing. The notch names the product a few pixels away, lit, with its ramp attached, so
             the watermark was the same fact said twice and worse. (If a pane ever needs to stay identifiable
             with its notch HIDDEN, that is where a watermark would come back — as the empty state, not as a
             permanent overlay.)

             SAME OVERLAY GRID AS THE WATERMARKS USED: a 3x3 [*, gutter, *] laid over EXACTLY the WebView's
             rect (Row 0 + RowSpan 2, matching the WebView above), so its cells coincide with the page's
             pane rects — both sides split the same area the same way, both using PaneLayoutInfo.GutterPx.
             Each notch is placed in its cell by PaneLayoutInfo.CellOf via the x:Bind functions below; WHERE in
             the cell (alignment, margin, shadow edge) is PlacePaneSelectors' (the sketch above).

             ⚠️ The pane ARRANGEMENT (pane 0 = main = bottom-left) is expressed twice: here through CellOf,
             and in map.js paneRects() which lays out the real maps. Same rule, opposite sides of the WebView
             boundary — change both.

             ⚠️ NO IsHitTestVisible="False" on this grid, unlike the watermark grid it replaces: these are
             real controls now. The grid itself has no Background, so its EMPTY areas still hit-test straight
             through to the map — only the notches themselves catch the pointer. Declared BEFORE the bottom
             bar so the bar draws over it and stays clickable where the two overlap.

             ⚠️ NO SITE, NO SELECTOR (the user's call, 2026-11-04): a selector shows only while a radar site is selected
             (Radar.HasRadarLoop, Now and Past alike) or a ForeCast model draws (its read-only model form) — IsNotchShown.
             ⚠️ "Hidden" is Opacity 0 + not hit-testable, NOT Collapsed: the selector stays laid out, so the top bar's place
             search always knows its width (OnPaneSelectorSizeChanged). Visibility only drops a pane that isn't in the layout.
             ⚠️ ONE show/hide for all four now (View → Pane selectors, persisted) — the per-notch tabs went with
             the attachment (2026-11-01). They used to be four independent view-state toggles. -->
        <!-- ⚠️ THE SITE CHECK TOAST IS GONE from the map band: the announced site check now shows in the NowCast
             window's ACTIVITY EXPANDER (TemporalPaneActivityExpander, fed by BarActivityViewModel.WatchSiteCheck). Don't re-add it here. -->

        <Grid x:Name="PaneNotchLayer" Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2">
            <Grid.Resources>
                <!-- Compare with radar's corner labels (declared at the end of this grid). -->
                <Style x:Key="ComparePaneLabelStyle" TargetType="Border">
                    <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left"/>
                    <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Top"/>
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="12,12,0,0"/>
                    <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,3"/>
                    <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="4"/>
                    <Setter Property="IsHitTestVisible" Value="False"/>
                    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedBrush}"/>
                </Style>
            </Grid.Resources>
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind PaneGutter}"/> <!-- the groove -->
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                <RowDefinition Height="{x:Bind PaneGutter}"/>   <!-- the groove -->
                <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="Notch0" Edge="Top"
                            SizeChanged="OnPaneSelectorSizeChanged"
                            IsFloating="True"
                            ShowTab="False"
                            EdgeStyle="CastShadow"
                            IsRaised="True"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            VerticalAlignment="Top"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.Radar.Pane0.IsVisible), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Opacity="{x:Bind NotchOpacity(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsNotchShown(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.ColumnSpan="{x:Bind PaneColumnSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}">
                <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                    <comp:PaneNotchContent Pane="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Pane0}"
                                           Radar="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar}"
                                           Model="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange}"
                                           IsCompact="{x:Bind NotchCompact(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
            </ctl:OverlayBar>

            <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="Notch1" Edge="Top"
                            IsFloating="True"
                            ShowTab="False"
                            EdgeStyle="CastShadow"
                            IsRaised="True"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            VerticalAlignment="Top"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.Radar.Pane1.IsVisible), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Opacity="{x:Bind NotchOpacity(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsNotchShown(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.ColumnSpan="{x:Bind PaneColumnSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}">
                <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                    <comp:PaneNotchContent Pane="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Pane1}"
                                           Radar="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar}"
                                           Model="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange}"
                                           IsCompact="{x:Bind NotchCompact(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
            </ctl:OverlayBar>

            <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="Notch2" Edge="Top"
                            IsFloating="True"
                            ShowTab="False"
                            EdgeStyle="CastShadow"
                            IsRaised="True"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            VerticalAlignment="Top"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.Radar.Pane2.IsVisible), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Opacity="{x:Bind NotchOpacity(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsNotchShown(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 2), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 2), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 2), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.ColumnSpan="{x:Bind PaneColumnSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 2), Mode=OneWay}">
                <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                    <comp:PaneNotchContent Pane="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Pane2}"
                                           Radar="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar}"
                                           Model="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange}"
                                           IsCompact="{x:Bind NotchCompact(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
            </ctl:OverlayBar>

            <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="Notch3" Edge="Top"
                            IsFloating="True"
                            ShowTab="False"
                            EdgeStyle="CastShadow"
                            IsRaised="True"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            VerticalAlignment="Top"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.Radar.Pane3.IsVisible), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Opacity="{x:Bind NotchOpacity(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsNotchShown(ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 3), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 3), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 3), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Grid.ColumnSpan="{x:Bind PaneColumnSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 3), Mode=OneWay}">
                <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                    <comp:PaneNotchContent Pane="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.Pane3}"
                                           Radar="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar}"
                                           Model="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange}"
                                           IsCompact="{x:Bind NotchCompact(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
            </ctl:OverlayBar>

            <!-- COMPARE WITH RADAR's pane labels (ShortRange.IsCompareActive only): which side is which, in each pane's
                 TOP-LEFT corner — "KTLX · live radar" | "HRRR 15Z · valid 6:00 PM". Words only, click-through. -->
            <Border x:Name="CompareRadarPaneLabel"
                    Style="{StaticResource ComparePaneLabelStyle}"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind CompareLabelVisibility(ViewModel.ShortRange.IsCompareActive), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}">
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind RadarPaneLabel(ViewModel.Radar.SelectedRadarOption), Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="12" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
            </Border>
            <Border x:Name="CompareModelPaneLabel"
                    Style="{StaticResource ComparePaneLabelStyle}"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind CompareLabelVisibility(ViewModel.ShortRange.IsCompareActive), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.Row="{x:Bind PaneRow(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.Column="{x:Bind PaneColumn(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                    Grid.RowSpan="{x:Bind PaneRowSpan(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}">
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange.ModelPaneLabel, Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="12" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
            </Border>
        </Grid>

        <!-- LOOP HOLDING GATE — PastCast's loading screen (Composites/LoopHoldingGate). It dims the map and the pane
             notches and swallows their input while a loop loads; the top bar, the map-tools rail and the floating console
             (all declared AFTER it) paint over it and stay live (the rail's tools grey through AreControlsLocked).
             Transparent and click-through while hidden. There is no bottom chrome any more (2026-11-04), so its
             ContentBottomInset stays 0 and the screen centres on the whole map.
             ⚠️ The TEMPORAL PANES are declared after it — harmless, because every pane steps aside while the gate's frost
             is up (MapViewModel.OnLoadingScreenChanged), so the gate never has a pane to dim. -->
        <comp:LoopHoldingGate x:Name="LoopGate" Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2" ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LoopGate}"/>

        <!-- ===== TOP MENU BAR (the user's call, 2026-11-01) =====

               ┌ Atlas View Settings Temporal Mode Pane Mode Isolation ── [ Search places ✕ ⌕ ] ── drag ── – □ ✕ ┐  46 tall
               └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  full width
                 ░░░ light cast shadow ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░    ALWAYS shown

             An OverlayBar (Edge Top, full width) over the map — it never resizes the map.
             ⚠️ NO "Menu" TAB (removed 2026-11-04, the user's call: "I don't want the user to hide this bar yet, not this way").
               The bar always shows; MapViewModel.IsMenuBarVisible is still persisted but nothing binds it now.
             • Atlas / Settings: plain items, a click opens or closes that window (they were the bottom bar's keys).
             • Temporal Mode: NowCast, ForeCast ─ PastCast; toggles the MODE (was the bar's three keys).
             • Pane Mode: Single / Double / Quad Pane (was the tools strip's pane-layout key). Isolation: the isolation
               picker drawn as a menu title (was the tools strip's picker). Both grey while the loop holding gate is up.
             • View: the three temporal panes (TogglePane: a running mode's pane open ⇄ hidden; while Now OR Fore runs, the
               other's item turns that mode on), then Pane selectors. Ctrl+1/2/3 = the panes. An item that can't act is
               DISABLED (CanPick*Pane) with "Turn on X first" in its shortcut column.
             • The EMPTY run is the window's CAPTION (drag, double-click maximize, snap) — MainWindow.UpdateCaptionBand
               sets the bar's rect as the Caption region; the menu items (MenuBarMenus) and the caption key are Passthrough holes.
             • The caption key (– □ ✕) is back where Windows puts it (it was the bottom bar's far-right key).
             ⚠️ DECLARED AFTER THE LOOP GATE (stays live over the frost) and BEFORE the temporal panes, which
             start at its bottom edge (OnTopChromeSizeChanged) and so cover its shadow over their own width.
             ⚠️ Every flyout here is ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False" (windowed), like the strip's — else the owned
             panel windows paint over it. -->
        <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="TopChrome"
                        Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2"
                        VerticalAlignment="Top"
                        Edge="Top"
                        ShowTab="False"
                        EdgeStyle="CastShadow"
                        SizeChanged="OnTopChromeSizeChanged"
                        PointerEntered="OnTopChromePointerEntered"
                        PointerExited="OnTopChromePointerExited"
                        GotFocus="OnTopChromeGotFocus">
            <!-- FULL SCREEN: the bar slides up out of sight on this (TopChromeSlideIn / Out); 0 = in place. -->
            <ctl:OverlayBar.RenderTransform>
                <TranslateTransform x:Name="TopChromeSlide"/>
            </ctl:OverlayBar.RenderTransform>
            <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                <!-- MinHeight 32 = the caption height; the CENTRED place search makes it taller (its box + 7 px above and
                     below, the tools strip's old margins — the user's call, 2026-11-03). -->
                <Grid x:Name="MenuBarContent" MinHeight="32">
                    <Grid.Resources>
                        <!-- A menu title: flat text button, full bar height, the stock hover. -->
                        <Style x:Key="MenuBarTitleButtonStyle" TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultButtonStyle}">
                            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
                            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
                            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="12,0"/>
                            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="4"/>
                            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
                            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,3"/>
                            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
                        </Style>
                    </Grid.Resources>
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- menus -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>    <!-- the caption (drag) run -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- – □ ✕ -->
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                    <!-- ORDER: Atlas · View · Settings (the user's call, 2026-11-03). Atlas and Settings are plain items that
                         OPEN or CLOSE their window on click (they were the bottom bar's window latches); View is the one menu. -->
                    <StackPanel x:Name="MenuBarMenus" Orientation="Horizontal">
                        <!-- ⚠️ Always opens on RADAR SITES (ToggleAtlasFromBar, the user's call 2026-10-01); PastCast's
                             button opens on Past events. -->
                        <Button x:Name="AtlasMenuButton" Content="Atlas" Style="{StaticResource MenuBarTitleButtonStyle}"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Anvil Atlas — radar sites and past events"
                                Click="OnAtlasMenuClick"/>
                        <Button x:Name="ViewMenuButton" Content="View" Style="{StaticResource MenuBarTitleButtonStyle}">
                            <Button.Flyout>
                                <MenuFlyout Placement="BottomEdgeAlignedLeft" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewPastPaneItem" Text="PastCast pane"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsPastPaneOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.CanPickPastPane, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind PastPaneAccel(ViewModel.CanPickPastPane), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnViewPastPaneClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                            <KeyboardAccelerator Modifiers="Control" Key="Number1"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewNowPaneItem" Text="NowCast pane"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsNowPaneOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.CanPickNowPane, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind NowPaneAccel(ViewModel.CanPickNowPane), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnViewNowPaneClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                            <KeyboardAccelerator Modifiers="Control" Key="Number2"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewForePaneItem" Text="ForeCast pane"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsForePaneOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.CanPickForePane, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind ForePaneAccel(ViewModel.CanPickForePane), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnViewForePaneClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                            <KeyboardAccelerator Modifiers="Control" Key="Number3"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.KeyboardAccelerators>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                    <MenuFlyoutSeparator/>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewPaneSelectorsItem" Text="Pane selectors"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ArePaneSelectorsVisible, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewRadarConsoleItem" Text="Radar console"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsRadarConsoleVisible, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                                    <!-- The tools strip had its own "Tools" tab until 2026-11-03; this item replaced it. -->
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewMapToolsItem" Text="Map tools"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsMapControlsStripVisible, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
                                    <MenuFlyoutSeparator/>
                                    <!-- FULL SCREEN (2026-11-04): never remembered — the app always starts windowed. IsChecked is
                                         set from code (SetFullScreen), the key is the root grid's F11 accelerator. -->
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="ViewFullScreenItem" Text="Full screen"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="F11"
                                                          Click="OnViewFullScreenClick"/>
                                </MenuFlyout>
                            </Button.Flyout>
                        </Button>
                        <Button x:Name="SettingsMenuButton" Content="Settings" Style="{StaticResource MenuBarTitleButtonStyle}"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Settings — map, radar, storage"
                                Click="OnSettingsMenuClick"/>
                        <!-- ===== TEMPORAL MODE (the user's call, 2026-11-03 — mock-up C; it replaced the bottom bar's three keys) =====

                               ┌ Temporal Mode · Now + Fore ┐   title names the RUNNING modes (just "Temporal Mode" when none)
                               │ ✓ NowCast       pane hidden │   right column = the mode runs but View hid its pane
                               │ ✓ ForeCast                  │
                               │ ─────────────────────────── │   the rule: Now + Fore together, Past ALONE
                               │   PastCast        (dimmed)  │   the side that's OFF dims while the other side runs…
                               │   Turns NowCast and ForeCast off   …and this greyed line says what clicking it does
                               └─────────────────────────────┘
                             A click toggles THAT MODE only (MapViewModel.ToggleTemporalMode); its pane follows the mode. The
                             dimmed side still works — dimming warns, it never blocks — and LIFTS to full strength under the
                             pointer / keyboard focus (OnModeItemLift / Settle) so it reads as clickable, not disabled.
                             ⚠️ THIS is the only place a mode turns on/off (2026-11-03); View's pane items only hide/show
                             (one looser case: Now ⇄ Fore, MapViewModel.TogglePane). -->
                        <Button x:Name="TemporalModeMenuButton" Style="{StaticResource MenuBarTitleButtonStyle}"
                                Content="{x:Bind TemporalModeTitle(ViewModel.IsNowCast, ViewModel.IsForeCast, ViewModel.IsPastCast), Mode=OneWay}">
                            <Button.Flyout>
                                <MenuFlyout Placement="BottomEdgeAlignedLeft" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="TemporalNowCastItem" Text="NowCast"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsNowCast, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Opacity="{x:Bind DimWhen(ViewModel.IsPastCast), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind PaneHiddenTag(ViewModel.IsNowPaneHidden), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnTemporalNowCastClick"
                                                          PointerEntered="OnModeItemLift" PointerExited="OnModeItemSettle"
                                                          GotFocus="OnModeItemLift" LostFocus="OnModeItemSettle"/>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="TemporalForeCastItem" Text="ForeCast"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsForeCast, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Opacity="{x:Bind DimWhen(ViewModel.IsPastCast), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind PaneHiddenTag(ViewModel.IsForePaneHidden), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnTemporalForeCastClick"
                                                          PointerEntered="OnModeItemLift" PointerExited="OnModeItemSettle"
                                                          GotFocus="OnModeItemLift" LostFocus="OnModeItemSettle"/>
                                    <MenuFlyoutSeparator/>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="TemporalPastCastItem" Text="PastCast"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsPastCast, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Opacity="{x:Bind DimWhenEither(ViewModel.IsNowCast, ViewModel.IsForeCast), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          KeyboardAcceleratorTextOverride="{x:Bind PaneHiddenTag(ViewModel.IsPastPaneHidden), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnTemporalPastCastClick"
                                                          PointerEntered="OnModeItemLift" PointerExited="OnModeItemSettle"
                                                          GotFocus="OnModeItemLift" LostFocus="OnModeItemSettle"/>
                                    <MenuFlyoutItem x:Name="TemporalModeHintItem" IsEnabled="False"
                                                    Text="{x:Bind TemporalModeHint(ViewModel.IsNowCast, ViewModel.IsForeCast, ViewModel.IsPastCast), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                    Visibility="{x:Bind TemporalModeHintVisibility(ViewModel.IsNowCast, ViewModel.IsForeCast, ViewModel.IsPastCast), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                </MenuFlyout>
                            </Button.Flyout>
                        </Button>

                        <!-- ===== PANE MODE (the user's call, 2026-11-04 — it replaced the tools strip's square pane-layout key) =====

                               ┌ Pane Mode ─────────┐
                               │   ▭  Single Pane    │   ToggleMenuFlyoutItems, the CURRENT one ticked; the marks are
                               │ ✓ ▭▭ Double Pane    │   drawn PathIcons (solid blocks, like the old key's list)
                               │   ⊞  Quad Pane      │
                               └─────────────────────┘
                             ⚠️ IsChecked is ONE-WAY and RE-ASSERTED in OnPaneModeClick: a same / refused pick changes no
                             property, so the clicked item would stay flipped. Greyed while the PastCast loading screen is up
                             (Radar.AreControlsLocked) — a layout change mid-load is a real memory risk. -->
                        <Button x:Name="PaneModeMenuButton" Content="Pane Mode" Style="{StaticResource MenuBarTitleButtonStyle}"
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}">
                            <Button.Flyout>
                                <MenuFlyout Placement="BottomEdgeAlignedLeft" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="PaneModeSingleItem" Text="Single Pane" Tag="Single"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsPaneLayout(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 0), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnPaneModeClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                            <PathIcon Data="M2,4 H16 V14 H2 Z"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="PaneModeDoubleItem" Text="Double Pane" Tag="TwoAcross"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsPaneLayout(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 1), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnPaneModeClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                            <PathIcon Data="M2,4 H8.5 V14 H2 Z M9.5,4 H16 V14 H9.5 Z"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                    <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem x:Name="PaneModeQuadItem" Text="Quad Pane" Tag="Quad"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsPaneLayout(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, 2), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                          Click="OnPaneModeClick">
                                        <ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                            <PathIcon Data="M2,4 H8.5 V8.5 H2 Z M9.5,4 H16 V8.5 H9.5 Z M2,9.5 H8.5 V14 H2 Z M9.5,9.5 H16 V14 H9.5 Z"/>
                                        </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem.Icon>
                                    </ToggleMenuFlyoutItem>
                                </MenuFlyout>
                            </Button.Flyout>
                        </Button>

                        <!-- ===== ISOLATION (the user's call, 2026-11-04 — it was the tools strip's isolation picker) =====

                               Isolation              a SectionedComboBox drawn as a MENU TITLE (IsMenuTitle): flat words,
                             ┌───────────────────┐    lit on hover / while open. The dropdown is the picker's own, unchanged:
                             │ No Isolation      │ ┐  the three MODES pinned above a rule, the 52 places scrolling below,
                             │ Isolate CONUS     │ │  capped at the picker's MaxDropDownHeight (360, its default — the
                             │ Select to Isolate │ ┘  height it had on the strip), 220 wide (DropDownWidth).
                             │───────────────────│
                             │ Alabama         ⋮ │    ⚠️ "Select to Isolate" ARMS the map — a MODE, not a resting choice:
                             └───────────────────┘    hovering a state highlights it; the click picks it (states.js).
                             ⚠⚠ A SectionedComboBox, NOT a ComboBox / MenuFlyout: a closed ComboBox cycles on the mousewheel
                             (it froze the map), and a MenuFlyout can't pin a section over a scrolling list. -->
                        <ctl:SectionedComboBox x:Name="IsolationMenuPicker"
                                               IsMenuTitle="True"
                                               PlaceholderText="Isolation"
                                               DropDownPlacement="BottomEdgeAlignedLeft"
                                               DropDownWidth="220"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                                               Margin="0,3"
                                               IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                               PinnedItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationModes, Mode=OneWay}"
                                               ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationPlaces, Mode=OneWay}"
                                               SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.SelectedIsolationOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                               ToolTipService.ToolTip="Mask the map down to CONUS or a single state">
                            <ctl:SectionedComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                                <!-- One isolation row, for BOTH sections. The modes carry hover text; the places have a null
                                     Tooltip, which shows nothing rather than an empty box. -->
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:StateIsolationOption">
                                    <Grid Background="Transparent" ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind Tooltip}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Label}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    </Grid>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </ctl:SectionedComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                        </ctl:SectionedComboBox>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- PLACE SEARCH, CENTRED on the window (spans every column; declared before the caption key so the
                         window buttons stay on top in a very narrow window). A Passthrough hole (UpdateNotchInputRegions). -->
                    <!-- Width: AS WIDE AS THE SINGLE-PANE SELECTOR right under it (OnPaneSelectorSizeChanged, the user's
                         call 2026-11-03); other layouts keep the last single-pane width. 236 is only the first value. -->
                    <comp:PlaceSearchBox x:Name="PlaceSearchBox"
                                         Width="236"
                                         Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                         HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                         Margin="0,7"
                                         ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>

                    <ctl:WindowCaptionKey x:Name="CaptionKey"
                                          Grid.Column="2"
                                          MinimizeRequested="OnCaptionMinimize"
                                          MaximizeRestoreRequested="OnCaptionMaximizeRestore"
                                          CloseRequested="OnCaptionClose"/>
                </Grid>
            </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
        </ctl:OverlayBar>

        <!-- ===== TEMPORAL PANES ===== (TemporalPanes/TemporalPane — one class, three declarations, Mode set here ONCE)

               ┌─────────────────────────── top menu bar ────────────────────────┐
               ├──────────┬──┬────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────┤
               │ PastCast │▤ │                                        │ ForeCast │  each 480 wide (Styles.xaml
               │    or    │⛶ │           …the map…                    │          │  TemporalPaneWidth), flush to
               │ NowCast  │↻ │                                        │          │  its edge and the TOP BAR's foot,
               │ (left)   │◍ │                                        │ (right)  │  down to the WINDOW BOTTOM (no
               │          │⊚ │                                        │          │  bottom chrome since 2026-11-04)
               └──────────┴──┴────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────┘
                           ↑ the MAP-TOOLS RAIL (below), docked to the left pane, or the window edge without one

             OVERLAYS, not OS windows: they never resize or push the map. Past and Now share the LEFT edge, safe only
             because Past excludes Now. Each shows while its mode runs AND it isn't HIDDEN from the top bar's View menu
             (MapViewModel.Is{Past,Now,Fore}PaneShown — also held back by the launch order and the loop holding gate) and
             builds its body on first show (see TemporalPane). The layer's TOP margin is the top bar's surface height
             (OnTopChromeSizeChanged); its bottom is the window's. The grid has no Background: between the panes the map
             still takes the pointer. Declared after the notches (a pane covers a notch it overlaps, as the windows
             did) and after the top bar, so an open pane covers the bar's cast shadow over its own width.
             (The panes no longer reach into the caption band: the TOP BAR is the caption now, and they start below it.) -->
        <Grid x:Name="TemporalPaneLayer" Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2">
            <tp:TemporalPane x:Name="TemporalPanePastCast" Mode="Past"
                             Width="{StaticResource TemporalPaneWidth}" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                             Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.IsPastPaneShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                             ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>
            <tp:TemporalPane x:Name="TemporalPaneNowCast" Mode="Now"
                             Width="{StaticResource TemporalPaneWidth}" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                             Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.IsNowPaneShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                             ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>
            <tp:TemporalPane x:Name="TemporalPaneForeCast" Mode="Fore"
                             Width="{StaticResource TemporalPaneWidth}" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                             Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.IsForePaneShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                             ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>

            <!-- ===== THE MAP-TOOLS RAIL (the user's call, 2026-11-04 — it replaced the horizontal bottom tools strip) =====

                   ┌ top menu bar ────────────────────────────    ┌ top menu bar ──────────────────────────────────
                   ├──┐                                           ├──────────┬──┐
                   │  │░                                          │ NowCast  │  │░
                   │▤▸│░  ← map layers (key + car)                │    or    │▤▸│░   DOCKED to the left pane's
                   │⁘ │░                                          │ PastCast │⁘ │░   RIGHT edge while Now or
                   │⛶ │░  ← fit to view                           │          │⛶ │░   Past's pane shows
                   │↻ │░  ← reset north                           │          │↻ │░   (MapToolsRailMargin)
                   │⁘ │░                                          │          │⁘ │░
                   │◍ │░  ← markers (placeholder)                 │          │◍ │░
                   │⊚ │░  ← location                              │          │⊚ │░
                   │  │░                                          │          │  │░
                   └──┘ no left pane: the window's left edge      └──────────┴──┘
                   48 wide, the top bar's foot to the window bottom (this layer's margins), the tools CENTRED top to
                   bottom (Composites/MapControlsStrip). RAISED face; its map side casts the light 14 px shade
                   (ShadowFadeLeft), or — EDGE-HATCH (bolt-on) — the hatch instead. View → Map tools hides it.
                   ⚠️ IN THIS LAYER ON PURPOSE: it shares the panes' top/bottom insets, and declared after them it covers a
                   left pane's map-side hatch (the rail is the map side then). Past and Now never show together. -->
            <Grid x:Name="MapToolsRail"
                  Width="48"
                  HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                  Margin="{x:Bind MapToolsRailMargin(ViewModel.IsPastPaneShown, ViewModel.IsNowPaneShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                  Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.IsMapControlsStripVisible), Mode=OneWay}">
                <Rectangle x:Name="MapToolsRailShadow"
                           Width="14" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,0,-14,0"
                           Fill="{StaticResource ShadowFadeLeft}"
                           Opacity="{ThemeResource OverlayBarShadowOpacity}"
                           IsHitTestVisible="False"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind HiddenWhen(ViewModel.EdgeHatch.IsHatch), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <!-- EDGE-HATCH (experimental bolt-on): the hatch on the rail's map side, in place of the shade. -->
                <ctl:EdgeHatch x:Name="EdgeHatchMapToolsRail"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                               Direction="Right"
                               Raised="True"
                               IsHitTestVisible="False"
                               Width="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Width, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Margin="{x:Bind MapToolsRailHatchMargin(ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Width), Mode=OneWay}"
                               Spacing="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Spacing, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Weight="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Weight, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Thin="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Thins, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Fade="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.Fades, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Dots="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.IsDots, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Ink="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.ColorHex, Mode=OneWay}"
                               LineOpacity="{x:Bind ViewModel.EdgeHatch.LineOpacity, Mode=OneWay}"
                               Visibility="{x:Bind PaneVisibility(ViewModel.EdgeHatch.IsHatch), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <Border x:Name="MapToolsRailSurface" Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedBrush}"/>
                <comp:MapControlsStrip x:Name="ToolsStrip"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                       ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>
            </Grid>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ===== THE FLOATING RADAR CONSOLE (the user's call, 2026-11-03 — canvas option C, "mirror") =====

                 ┌ Menu bar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                 │◗│                            ╭──────────────────╮   ← floating pane selector(s)
                 │▤│
                 │⛶│                ...map...
                 │↻│                ╭──────────────────────────────╮
                 │◍│                │  ⌂ KTLX  Oklahoma City     ˅ │      ← the SITE TAB (RadarConsoleSiteTab), centred
                 │⊚│ ╭──────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴───────────╮
                 │⌕│ │ 1:07 PM  ▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮ scrubber ▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮  ◀ ▶ ▶ ↺  VCP: 212    │  ← THIS: the console exactly as it
                 │◎│ │ 2 min ago                              3/10      Mode: precip │    was on the bar, rounded, floating
                 │ │ ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
                 └─┘ ↑ the map-tools rail (left)                                     SelectorGap above the window bottom

             Centred on the window (play = the midpoint, RadarControls.CentreOnPlay), SelectorGap (8) above the window
             bottom — there is no bottom chrome since 2026-11-04 (its tools are the left RAIL). Same look as
             the bar it came from: the GROUND surface, NOT raised (the selectors are raised). It never shrinks: in a window
             too narrow for both edge panes it overlaps their bottoms — DECLARED AFTER the temporal panes so it paints over
             them and stays clickable, and after the loop holding gate, so it stays live over the frost like the bar did.
             View → Radar console hides it (IsRadarConsoleVisible, persisted).
             ⚠️ NO SITE, NO CONSOLE (the user's call, 2026-11-04): in NowCast AND PastCast it shows only while a radar site
             is selected (Radar.HasRadarLoop) — pick a site on the map to bring it up. The one exception is MODEL MODE
             (ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown): ModelConsole plays a ForeCast run here with or without a site.
             (MainWindow.ConsoleVisibility.)
             ⚠️ THE SITE TAB IS BACK (2026-11-04, the user's call): the console's short-lived TOP ROW (RadarConsoleHeader:
             networks · site · Inspect + rings/ruler) is gone — its tools moved to the map-tools rail, leaving only the site
             picker, so it stands on the console as a tab again. Centred by layout, so nothing is measured.
             ⚠️ MODEL MODE: while ForeCast's Short Range draws, ModelConsole plays the run IN THIS SAME CELL, over
             RadarControls — NOT while comparing with radar (ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown): then radar's console runs and
             the model follows it. RadarControls stays LAID OUT underneath (Opacity 0, not hit-testable — never Collapsed),
             so the console keeps its width, and ModelConsole has its exact widths.
             ⚠️ CENTRED ONLY BECAUSE IT IS A FIXED WIDTH: the clock reserves a two-digit hour (RadarControls). -->
        <Grid x:Name="ConsoleIslandHost"
              Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2"
              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
              VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
              Margin="0,0,0,8"
              Visibility="{x:Bind ConsoleVisibility(ViewModel.IsRadarConsoleVisible, ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarLoop, ViewModel.ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown), Mode=OneWay}">
            <!-- The host: the SITE TAB (row 0, Composites/RadarConsoleSiteTab, centred) standing on the console (row 1).
                 ⚠️ The tab is declared AFTER the console so it paints over the console's top hairline: its -3 bottom margin
                 reaches 3 px INTO the console (not 1 — at a display scale above 100% the hairline lands on fractional pixels and
                 a 1 px overlap let it show as a line under the tab); the tab pads +2 at its foot so its content doesn't move.
                 Its own halo stops at its foot, so neither shadow crosses the other plate. -->
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the site tab -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the console -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <ctl:OverlayBar x:Name="ConsoleIsland"
                        Grid.Row="1"
                        Edge="Bottom"
                        IsFloating="True"
                        ShowTab="False"
                        EdgeStyle="CastShadow">
            <ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
                <Grid x:Name="ConsoleIslandContent">
                    <comp:RadarControls x:Name="TimeModule"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Opacity="{x:Bind RadarConsoleOpacity(ViewModel.ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                                        IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsRadarConsoleLive(ViewModel.ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                                        ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar}"/>
                    <comp:ModelConsole x:Name="ModelConsole"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Visibility="{x:Bind ModelConsoleVisibility(ViewModel.ShortRange.IsModelConsoleShown), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       UseDotMatrix="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsDotMatrixScrubber, Mode=OneWay}"
                                       UseHatch="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsHatchScrubber, Mode=OneWay}"
                                       HatchLook="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HatchLook}"
                                       ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange.Playback}"/>
                </Grid>
            </ctl:OverlayBar.BarContent>
        </ctl:OverlayBar>
        <comp:RadarConsoleSiteTab x:Name="RadarConsoleSiteTab"
                                  Grid.Row="0"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                  Margin="0,0,0,-3"
                                  ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel}"/>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ===== FULL SCREEN — the REVEAL STRIP and the HINT (2026-11-04; rules at MainWindow.xaml.cs FULL SCREEN) =====

               ▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁   ← REVEAL STRIP: 3 px, invisible, the full width of the screen's
                     ╭──────────────────────────────────╮      top edge; the pointer resting on it ~150 ms slides the menu
                     │ Full screen · pointer to the top │      bar down (the map is a WebView, which never tells XAML about
                     │ for the menu · F11 or Esc to exit│      the pointer — so this strip is the only way to see it there)
                     ╰──────────────────────────────────╯   ← the HINT, ~3 s on entering, click-through
             ⚠️ DECLARED LAST so the strip lies over the panes, the rail and the console too (in full screen they all start at
             the screen's top). Collapsed outside full screen and while the bar is down. -->
        <Border x:Name="FullScreenRevealStrip"
                Height="3"
                VerticalAlignment="Top"
                Background="Transparent"
                Visibility="Collapsed"
                PointerEntered="OnRevealStripPointerEntered"
                PointerExited="OnRevealStripPointerExited"/>
        <Border x:Name="FullScreenHint"
                HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                VerticalAlignment="Top"
                Margin="0,28,0,0"
                Padding="16,10"
                CornerRadius="8"
                Opacity="0"
                IsHitTestVisible="False"
                Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedBrush}"
                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"
                BorderThickness="1">
            <TextBlock Text="Full screen · move the pointer to the top for the menu · press F11 or Esc to exit"
                       FontSize="13"
                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</Window>
